{"id":"d17fa79941daf650","group":"58","path":"58/batch12/58-df-fodor.md","title":"Fodor's Lemma","display":"df-fodor — Fodor's Lemma","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-fodor","aliases":["58-df-fodor","Fodor's Lemma"],"display":"df-fodor — Fodor's Lemma","depends_on":["[[58-df-ordinal]]","[[58-df-regressive-function]]","[[58-df-stationary]]","[[58-df-regular-cardinal]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-fodor"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-fodor</span><span>Fodor's Lemma</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-fodor — Fodor's Lemma"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"5582a281f15a33c2\" href=\"?note=5582a281f15a33c2\" title=\"58-df-ordinal\">58-df-ordinal</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"aa5065a1f0bd9a7f\" href=\"?note=aa5065a1f0bd9a7f\" title=\"58-df-regressive-function\">58-df-regressive-function</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"b802c3dd76418d95\" href=\"?note=b802c3dd76418d95\" title=\"58-df-stationary\">58-df-stationary</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"0fbfc19800246e77\" href=\"?note=0fbfc19800246e77\" title=\"58-df-regular-cardinal\">58-df-regular-cardinal</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span> (regular uncountable cardinal, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"0fbfc19800246e77\" href=\"?note=0fbfc19800246e77\" title=\"58-df-regular-cardinal\">58-df-regular-cardinal</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{FodorPrinciple}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{FodorPrinciple}_S\\)</span> (Fodor principle predicate defined here)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Regressive}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Regressive}_S\\)</span> (regressive-function predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"aa5065a1f0bd9a7f\" href=\"?note=aa5065a1f0bd9a7f\" title=\"58-df-regressive-function\">58-df-regressive-function</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Stationary}\">\\(\\mathrm{Stationary}\\)</span> (stationarity predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"b802c3dd76418d95\" href=\"?note=b802c3dd76418d95\" title=\"58-df-stationary\">58-df-stationary</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S\\)</span> (regular-cardinal predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"0fbfc19800246e77\" href=\"?note=0fbfc19800246e77\" title=\"58-df-regular-cardinal\">58-df-regular-cardinal</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}fodor} \\vdash \\mathrm{FodorPrinciple}_S(\\kappa)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\omega&lt;\\kappa\\land\\forall S\\subseteq\\kappa\\;\\forall f:S\\to\\kappa\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Stationary}(S,\\kappa)\\land\\mathrm{Regressive}_S(f,S)\\to\\exists H\\subseteq S\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Stationary}(H,\\kappa)\\land\\forall\\xi,\\eta\\in H\\;(f(\\xi)=f(\\eta))\\bigr)\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}fodor} \\vdash \\mathrm{FodorPrinciple}_S(\\kappa)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\omega&lt;\\kappa\\land\\forall S\\subseteq\\kappa\\;\\forall f:S\\to\\kappa\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Stationary}(S,\\kappa)\\land\\mathrm{Regressive}_S(f,S)\\to\\exists H\\subseteq S\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Stationary}(H,\\kappa)\\land\\forall\\xi,\\eta\\in H\\;(f(\\xi)=f(\\eta))\\bigr)\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Fodor: regressive functions are constant on a stationary set (no need for measurability)</li>\n<li>Solovay: stronger version; partition to stationary many pieces each reflecting</li>\n<li>Pressing down: variant of Fodor; often used in set theory proofs</li>\n<li>Applications: Sacks rank, Silver's theorem on singular cardinals</li>\n<li>Regressive functions and stationary sets are upstream predicates.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Jech, Set Theory</li>\n<li>Kanamori, The Higher Infinite</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-ordinal","status":"resolved","id":"5582a281f15a33c2","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-ordinal]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-regressive-function","status":"resolved","id":"aa5065a1f0bd9a7f","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-regressive-function]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-stationary","status":"resolved","id":"b802c3dd76418d95","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-stationary]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-regular-cardinal","status":"resolved","id":"0fbfc19800246e77","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-regular-cardinal]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-regular-cardinal","status":"resolved","id":"0fbfc19800246e77","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\kappa$ (regular uncountable cardinal, see [[58-df-regular-cardinal]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-regressive-function","status":"resolved","id":"aa5065a1f0bd9a7f","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Regressive}_S$ (regressive-function predicate, see [[58-df-regressive-function]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-stationary","status":"resolved","id":"b802c3dd76418d95","anchor":"ref-7","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Stationary}$ (stationarity predicate, see [[58-df-stationary]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-regular-cardinal","status":"resolved","id":"0fbfc19800246e77","anchor":"ref-8","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S$ (regular-cardinal predicate, see [[58-df-regular-cardinal]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\kappa","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{FodorPrinciple}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Regressive}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Stationary}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}fodor} \\vdash \\mathrm{FodorPrinciple}_S(\\kappa)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\omega<\\kappa\\land\\forall S\\subseteq\\kappa\\;\\forall f:S\\to\\kappa\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Stationary}(S,\\kappa)\\land\\mathrm{Regressive}_S(f,S)\\to\\exists H\\subseteq S\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Stationary}(H,\\kappa)\\land\\forall\\xi,\\eta\\in H\\;(f(\\xi)=f(\\eta))\\bigr)\\Bigr)","display":true}],"bytes":1587,"backlinks":[{"id":"1d6484d05365d55f","anchor":"ref-1","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-539","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch12/58-df-fodor.md|58-df-fodor]]（batch12）"}],"outgoing":["5582a281f15a33c2","aa5065a1f0bd9a7f","b802c3dd76418d95","0fbfc19800246e77"]}